does (?i) match?          rust crates, anchored
pattern   subject                                        regex fancy
k         U+004B LATIN CAPITAL LETTER K                  yes   yes
k         U+212A KELVIN SIGN                             yes   yes
s         U+017F LATIN SMALL LETTER LONG S               yes   yes
U+00DF    U+1E9E LATIN CAPITAL LETTER SHARP S            yes   yes
U+1E9E    U+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S              yes   yes
ss        U+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S              no    no
[k]       U+212A KELVIN SIGN                             yes   yes
[a-z]     U+212A KELVIN SIGN                             yes   yes
i         U+0131 LATIN SMALL LETTER DOTLESS I            no    no
i         U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE   no    no
i U+0307  U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE   no    no

does (?i) fold the BACKREFERENCE comparison too?
regex        (?i)(a)\1                  error: backreferences are not supported
fancy-regex  (?i)(a)\1  vs 'a' + U+0041   yes
fancy-regex  (?i)(k)\1  vs 'k' + U+212A   no

one program, two answers about the same pair
  to_uppercase(U+00DF) is 'SS'          true     regex (?i): no
  eq_ignore_ascii_case(U+00DF, 'ss')    false    regex (?i): no
  to_lowercase(U+212A) is 'k'           true     regex (?i): yes
  to_uppercase(U+017F) is 'S'           true     regex (?i): yes
  to_lowercase(U+1E9E) is U+00DF        true     regex (?i): yes
